{
 "_readme": [
  "Card scans TCGdex does not have. Every builder skips them up front, so the",
  "site never asks for one.",
  "",
  "THE SWEEP THAT FILLS THIS FILE IS scripts/sweep-scans.mjs AND IT READS THE",
  "BUILT TREE. Run it after a build; it makes tens of thousands of requests to",
  "TCGdex, so it is NOT in build-all.mjs and must not be added to it.",
  "",
  "  node scripts/sweep-scans.mjs              sweep public/, union the result",
  "  node scripts/sweep-scans.mjs --recheck    also re-test what is on file",
  "",
  "THE FIRST SWEEP WAS PARTIAL AND NOBODY COULD TELL. This file said it had",
  "checked 'every one of the 3,539 tcgdex image urls the site emits' on",
  "2026-08-14 and found 101. That was a list of pages somebody had in front of",
  "them rather than a rule, so it went stale the moment the tree grew. Re-swept",
  "on 2026-08-18 from public/ itself: 24,237 distinct card bases in the HTML,",
  "seven times the surface, plus another 6,326 that only appear in the JSON under",
  "public/data, which the search page and the games fetch and turn into <img>",
  "urls in the browser. 30,563 distinct bases, and 528 of them answer 404. The",
  "101 were 19% of it.",
  "",
  "So the input is now 'every assets.tcgdex.net url in public/', which cannot go",
  "stale the way a page list does: public/ IS what a reader gets.",
  "",
  "WHY IT MATTERS. Every one of these images carries onerror=\"this.remove()\", so",
  "nothing ever looked broken: the picture silently vanished and the reader got a",
  "card with a name and a rarity and a hole where the scan should be, at the cost",
  "of a dead round trip to find out. Skipping them renders the same tile without",
  "the gap and without the request.",
  "",
  "Entries are image BASES, so one covers /low and /high at both webp and avif.",
  "",
  "IT IS SAFE TO GO STALE IN ONE DIRECTION ONLY. An entry TCGdex has since",
  "backfilled costs one missing picture; a base that is missing from here costs a",
  "dead request on every page load. That is why the default is union and why",
  "dropping an entry needs --recheck and an actual 200.",
  "",
  "`deadUrls` is the same idea for images that are NOT TCGdex card scans, and it",
  "is maintained separately: sweep-scans.mjs reads it and writes it back",
  "untouched. The other three hosts were swept on 2026-08-14, 1,116 urls across",
  "i.ytimg.com, tcgplayer-cdn, images.pokemontcg.io and images.scrydex.com. Four",
  "answered 403 to both HEAD and GET, two TCGplayer products at two sizes each,",
  "while the other 275 TCGplayer images were fine, so it is those products rather",
  "than a bot block. Everything else on those three hosts answered 200.",
  "",
  "`checked` is the 2026-08-14 date for deadUrls. `basesChecked` is when",
  "sweep-scans.mjs last ran. They are not interchangeable."
 ],
